  "confidences": {"U": 0.7, "A": 0.7, "C": 0.6, "V": 0.7},
  "rationales": {
    "U": "证据片段：'before they will not be able to order the discontinued products'。解释：该短语使用否定和复杂结构，可能降低可理解性。",
    "A": "证据片段：'before they will not be able to order the discontinued products'。解释：'before'与'will not be able to'结合可能导致时间顺序歧义，不清楚适应期与产品停用的关系。",
    "C": "证据片段：'by the second quarter of 2004'。解释：指定了具体时间点，但需确认业务上下文中是否正确，可能过时或需澄清。",
    "V": "证据片段：'allowing customers the time to adjust'。解释：'time'未量化，无法客观验证是否允许足够调整时间，缺乏可测试性。"
  },
  "suggestions": {
    "U": "The new system must be operational by Q2 2004. Customers must have a period to adjust to the new scheme before the discontinued products become unavailable for ordering.",
    "A": "The new system must be in place by the second quarter of 2004. After the system is operational, customers will have a specified adjustment period. At the end of this period, ordering of discontinued products will be disabled.",
    "C": "保持不变",
    "V": "The new system must be deployed by June 30, 2004. Customers must be able to access the new system for at least 30 days before the ordering functionality for discontinued products is disabled on July 31, 2004."
  },
  "issues": [
    {
      "type": "A",
      "evidence": "before they will not be able to order the discontinued products",
      "rewrite": "After the system is operational, customers will have a specified adjustment period. At the end of this period, ordering of discontinued products will be disabled."
    },
    {
      "type": "V",
      "evidence": "allowing customers the time to adjust",
      "rewrite": "Customers must be able to access the new system for at least 30 days before the ordering functionality for discontinued products is disabled on a specified date."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "item": "R1",
  "scores": {"U": 2, "A": 2, "C": 3, "V": 1},
  "confidences": {"U": 0.9, "A": 0.95, "C": 0.8, "V": 0.95},
  "rationales": {"U":"'allowing customers the time to adjust to the new scheme before they will not be able to order the discontinued products' is a convoluted, passive, and temporally ambiguous clause; it obscures who defines 'time to adjust', how much time is required, and conflates deployment timing with business policy enforcement.", "A":"'the new system must be in place by the second quarter of 2004' lacks precision on what 'in place' means (installed? deployed? fully operational? user-accessible?); 'before they will not be able to order' uses double negative and future-in-future phrasing ('will not be able to') that contradicts the fixed deadline and introduces modal uncertainty.", "C":"The requirement implies causality between system deployment timing and product discontinuation eligibility, but does not specify whether product discontinuation is governed by the system’s go-live date or an independent business rule — this misaligns technical delivery with policy enforcement scope.", "V":"No testable condition is defined: there is no measurable criterion for 'in place', no quantified minimum adjustment period, no observable event marking when ordering of discontinued products becomes prohibited, and no way to objectively verify compliance without external policy documentation."},
  "suggestions": {"U":"Replace with atomic, active-voice statements specifying concrete deliverables and deadlines.", "A":"Define 'in place' as 'fully deployed, validated, and accessible to all authorized end users for production use', and replace 'before they will not be able to order' with a precise, date-bound business rule.", "C":"Clarify whether product discontinuation enforcement is a functional behavior of the new system or an external process; if the former, make it a separate functional requirement.", "V":"Rewrite to include at least one objectively verifiable condition (e.g., 'system shall reject orders for discontinued products submitted after 2004-06-30')."},
  "issues": [
    {"type":"U","evidence":"allowing customers the time to adjust to the new scheme before they will not be able to order the discontinued products","rewrite":"The system shall be fully deployed, validated, and available to all authorized customers by 2004-06-30."},
    {"type":"A","evidence":"must be in place by the second quarter of 2004","rewrite":"The system shall be fully deployed, validated, and accessible to all authorized end users for production use no later than 2004-06-30."},
    {"type":"V","evidence":"allowing customers the time to adjust to the new scheme before they will not be able to order the discontinued products","rewrite":"Effective 2004-07-01, the system shall reject any order containing discontinued products, as identified in the Product Discontinuation List v1.0 dated 2004-03-15."}
  ]
}
